@echasnovski I can get correct completion items for `ml-` without having to change `iskeyword` to include `-`
yes it come from `mini.completion` as there's no other auto completion installed

FYI here's my config:
```lua
require("mini.completion").setup {
	fallback_action = "<C-x><C-n>",
	process_items = function(items, base)
		-- Don't show 'Text' suggestions
		items = vim.tbl_filter(function(x)
			return x.kind ~= 1
		end, items)
		return MiniCompletion.default_process_items(items, base)
	end,
	window = {
		signature = { border = "single" },
	},
	lsp_completion = {
		source_func = "omnifunc",
	},
	delay = { signature = 10 ^ 7 },
}
```

@mortezadadgar, this use case should now be fixed on latest `main` *without* tweaking 'iskeyword'.

The culprit for this was that 'mini.completion' at the time completely didn't respect LSP server response when trying to compute completed word. It only computed based on the maximum keyword to the left of the cursor. But that was resolved in 21b3205eda2a7b0a50c3c04e4c127731969dcf81. That's why I somewhat assumed (in Matrix chat room) that this should have been already solved. But it wasn't, as that didn't recognize `itemDefaults` from `textDocument/completion` response. I was able to find this by indeed reproducing the issue and observing server responses.

I can no longer reproduce this locally. Could you please try the latest `main`?
